ll,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116269","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116269.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116269.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-24T15:34:27Z"},"body":"Alternative to PR #107838 which works with ImporterMesh instead of ArrayMesh. I was requested to change this because ImporterMesh is entirely self-contained on the CPU, while ArrayMesh communicates with the GPU.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI needed the ability to merge multiple meshes together into one mesh in a glTF context, and I searched the APIs of ArrayMesh, ImporterMesh, and SurfaceTool only to find that such a thing does not exist yet. This PR implements it.\r\n\r\nThis function will be important for https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4630. This PR does not expose anything in the editor for merging meshes, it just adds the underlying functionality to ImporterMesh. Because https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4630 exists I don't think I need to open a separate proposal for this, but a full solution to https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4630 will involve showing stuff in the editor.\r\n\r\nThis is a highly requested feature. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/182, https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/901, https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7970, https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12110, https://forum.godotengine.org/t/combining-meshes/55687, https://forum.godotengine.org/t/combine-multiple-meshinstance3d-into-1-meshinstance3d/88140, https://godotforums.org/d/32740-merging-array-meshessubtracting-from-array-meshes-with-csg, https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/nfc22a/how_to_join_3d_meshes_from_code/, and more.\r\n\r\nI have tested this PR on a simple mesh, including duplicating surfaces, deduplicating surfaces, negative scale, and positive scale, and at least in my testing it works correctly.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116269/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116269/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}